  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): セイロンニッケイ",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%BB%E3%82%A4%E3%83%AD%E3%83%B3%E3%83%8B%E3%83%83%E3%82%B1%E3%82%A4",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 106541715,
      "text": "セイロンニッケイ は、クスノキ科ニッケイ属に分類される常緑樹の1種である。その内樹皮は香辛料のシナモンの原料となり、この植物種自身もシナモンとよばれることがある。ニッケイ属の他のいくつかの種の樹皮由来の香辛料もシナモンとよばれるが、狭義のシナモンはセイロンニッケイを原料にするものを指し、英名では true cinnamon（真のシナモン）ともよばれる。学名の種小名である verum も、ラテン語で「真の」を意味する。Cinnamomum zeylanicum の学名が使われることも多い。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Cinnamomum verum",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnamomum_verum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1368745785,
      "text": "Cinnamomum verum, also known as true cinnamon or Ceylon cinnamon, is a small evergreen tree belonging to the family Lauraceae, native to Sri Lanka. The inner bark of the tree is historically regarded as the spice cinnamon, though this name has also been used for C. cassia (cassia) as well."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Cinnamomum verum",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnamomum_verum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 175600272,
      "text": "El árbol de la canela, conocido como canelo, es un árbol de hoja perenne, de 10 a 15 metros de altura, procedente de Sri Lanka. De su corteza interna se produce la especia canela, que se obtiene pelando y frotando las ramas."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Cannelier de Ceylan",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannelier_de_Ceylan",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 238586726,
      "text": "Le cannelier ou cannelier de Ceylan est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Lauraceae. C'est un arbre originaire du Sri Lanka."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Cinnamomum verum",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnamomum_verum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 71688286,
      "text": "Cinnamomum verum, comummente conhecida como caneleira-verdadeira e frequentemente designada pelo seu sinónimo taxonómico Cinnamomum zeylanicum, é uma espécie de pequenas árvores perenifólias da família das Lauráceas, nativa do Sri Lanka, sendo uma das espécies de cuja casca se produz a canela."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Kayu manis",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kayu_manis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 29841275,
      "text": "Kayu manis atau dengan nama ilmiah Cinnamomum ialah jenis pohon penghasil rempah-rempah. Di dalam kamus Biologi, Cinnamomum zeylanicum, termasuk ke dalam jenis rempah-rempah yang dihasilkan dari kulit bagian dalam yang kering, yang amat beraroma, manis, dan pedas. Orang biasa menggunakan rempah-rempah dalam makanan yang dibakar manis, anggur panas dan juga dipakai untuk keperluan medis."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Cinnamomum verum § Cultivation",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnamomum_verum#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 1368745785,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "The old botanical synonym for the tree, Cinnamomum zeylanicum, is derived from Sri Lanka's former name, Ceylon. Sri Lanka still produces 80–90% of the world's supply of C. verum; it is also cultivated on a commercial scale in the Seychelles, Madagascar and Tanzania.\nOn Borneo, Cinnamomum verum is cultivated at low elevations in Sarawak (Kuching District), Sabah (Keningau and Sandakan districts), and Kalimantan.\n\n■ Cultivars\nThere are several different cultivars of Cinnamomum verum based on the taste of bark:\n\nPani-Miris Kurundu - Sweet and spicy\nMiris Kurundu - Spicy\nSewele Kurundu - Smooth\nWeli Kurundu - Coarse\nThiththa Kurundu - Bitter",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "es": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (es): Cinnamomum verum § Cultivo",
        "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnamomum_verum#Cultivo",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 175600272,
        "heading": "Cultivo",
        "text": "El antiguo sinónimo botánico del árbol, Cinnamomum zeylanicum, deriva del antiguo nombre de Sri Lanka, Ceilán.​ Según una publicación de 2020, Sri Lanka produce el 90 % del suministro mundial de C. verum,​​ que también se cultiva a escala comercial en las Seychelles, Madagascar y Tanzania.​​",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
